{{ElectionsFL}}

The '''2024 United States House of Representatives elections in Florida''' were held on November 5, 2024, to elect the 28 [[United States House of Representatives|U.S. representatives]] from the [[U.S. state|state]] of [[Florida]], one from each of the state's [[Florida's congressional districts|congressional districts]]. The elections coincided with the [[2024 United States presidential election|U.S. presidential election]], [[2024 United States House of Representatives elections|other elections]] to the House of Representatives, [[2024 United States Senate elections|elections]] to the [[United States Senate]], and various [[2024 United States elections|state and local elections]]. Primary elections took place on August 20.

{{Horizontal TOC|nonum=yes|limit=2}}

==Background==
On September 2, 2023, a Florida judge ruled that Florida's congressional map, created by Governor [[Ron DeSantis]], violated the Florida Constitution and cannot be used for any future House elections.<ref name="ABC News unconstitutional">{{Cite web |last=Schneider |first=Mike |date=2023-09-02 |title=DeSantis' redistricting map in Florida is unconstitutional and must be redrawn, judge says |url=https://abcnews.go.com/US/wireStory/desantis-redistricting-map-florida-unconstitutional-redrawn-judge-102887623 |access-date=2023-09-04 |publisher=ABC News |language=en}}</ref> The issue was specifically on [[Florida's 5th congressional district|Florida's 5th district]], then represented by Democrat [[Al Lawson]], which was removed and replaced by a Republican-leaning district. This was controversial because the district had an African-American plurality.<ref name="ABC News unconstitutional" /> The state's successful appeal is to be challenged in front of the Florida Supreme Court, but a redrawn map was not created by election time. A concurrent federal lawsuit is also in progress.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2024-01-24 |title=Florida Supreme Court will consider challenge to DeSantis' redistricting map|url=https://edition.cnn.com/2024/01/24/politics/florida-supreme-court-agrees-to-take-up-congressional-redistricting-fight/index.html |access-date=2024-01-29 |website=CNN Politics|first=Gary|last=Fineout |language=en}}</ref>

